{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1060868-means-of-extending-mortal-life","id":1060868,"title":"Means of Extending Mortal Life","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-10T07:32:27-08:00","id":1060868,"title":"Means of Extending Mortal Life","content":"I was pondering one of my characters, and was wondering if anyone knew how many different ways there are to extend human life in cWoD? I'm generally aware of Vampirism, being ghouled, and that some sorcerer/Mage means are out there. I'm not sure I'd count Wraith for this thought process. Are there a lot of others out there or am I touching the main ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T08:21:14-08:00","id":1060889,"title":"","content":"If you want them to remain mortal, the only ways I know of are to use the Path of Alchemy (level 4 produces a regime that slows aging to one month for every year, so I figure it would be reasonable to have level 5 produce a regime that slows aging to one week for every years and to have level 6 produce a regime that grants functional immortality), to enter into a Soul Pact with a Demon Lord and purchase the Demonic Investment of Longevity and Youth, or to become the Ghoul of the Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T11:15:19-08:00","id":1060946,"title":"","content":"In mage you gain a permanent dot of paradox for each century you extend your life past normal human life spand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T14:03:19-08:00","id":1061015,"title":"","content":"Well, that is due to a weakness of True Magick. Other forms of life extention have other weaknesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T01:42:43-08:00","id":1061167,"title":"","content":"The standard inconveniences off a typical ST that get thrown at a immortal mortal should be enough for a couple of centuries worth of ppermadox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T02:09:47-08:00","id":1061173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1060868-means-of-extending-mortal-life?p=1061167#post1061167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The standard inconveniences off a typical ST that get thrown at a immortal mortal should be enough for a couple of centuries worth of ppermadox.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all fun in games till you have to roll backlash","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T02:31:13-08:00","id":1061176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1060868-means-of-extending-mortal-life?p=1061173#post1061173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's all fun in games till you have to roll backlash</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this is only of consequence in the Mageverse.<br /> If you are playing in some other setting, then I would avoid using Mage rules. Especially considering that a non mage would roll for backlash only once a century, starting at the fifth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T07:23:08-08:00","id":1061236,"title":"","content":"But I do not think that the longevity rules apply to non-Mages even in Mage the Ascension (every mention of permanent Paradox in relation to longevity have specifically referred to the effects of longevity on Mages).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T07:30:22-08:00","id":1061239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1060868-means-of-extending-mortal-life#post1060868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are there a lot of others out there or am I touching the main ones?</div> </div> </div> </div><u>For Changeling</u>:<br /> -Spend time in Freeholds where you don't age (that's from memory though, and may or may not apply once C20 comes out).<br /> -Age is also probably not a consideration in the Dreaming by extension. I would say certainly not in the Far Dreaming.<br /> <br /> <u>For Werewolf</u>:<br /> -For Humans: becoming Possessed is probably the most straight forward option, though you give up some free will in doing so.<br /> -For Fera: The Flux can almost certainly reverse aging, though in the vein of Mage there should be unexpected consequences.<br /> <br /> <u>Fera Specifics</u>:<br /> -Ananasi can (with Ananasa's blessing) eat their way to a younger body. Literally eat a younger person from the inside out and take over.<br /> -Rokea don't die of old age at all.<br /> -Kitsune double their lifespan for each rank attained. A typical 4th ranker should have around an 800 year lifespan (1600 for 5th and 3200 for Legends).<br /> -Both Mokole and Gurahl have Rites that allow them to sleep through the ages. Maybe not quite what you were looking for, but it technically extends their lifetimes.<br /> <br /> Edit: oh, and for Highlanders: don't get your head cut off (this one is obviously non canon joking <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 03-11-2017, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T07:42:51-08:00","id":1061242,"title":"","content":"Mokole also have various Gifts and rites to de-age themselves, like shedding bones and the Sleep of Hsi Wang Mu for the Middle Dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T08:51:24-08:00","id":1061259,"title":"","content":"I would figure disconnection would also prevent aging... but that is a bit extreme, and there is no guarantee a bigger umbral fish doesn't eat you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T08:54:43-08:00","id":1061260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1060868-means-of-extending-mortal-life?p=1061259#post1061259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would figure disconnection would also prevent aging... but that is a bit extreme, and there is no guarantee a bigger umbral fish doesn't eat you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. And that theoretically works on anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T10:20:26-08:00","id":1061283,"title":"","content":"Demons do not age as long as they have at least one Faith Point. (Demon Player's Guide p.15) By straining the Rules As Written this is one of a Demon's inherent powers, which can be granted through a Pact. Exactly how this would keep working is up for grabs: the Player's Guide says this is as long as a Demon has Faith Points. Since mortals don't have those, this can either cross over with their Faith rating or their Willpower. The more literal interpretation would require them to roll Willpower 7 for every scene they want to use this. But given the nature of a scene this becomes even muddier to use on a day-to-day basis.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller though I would not allow the granting of unagingness (so NOT immortality) without some serious sacrifices on the part of the Thrall, possibly making it more of a hassle than it's worth on their part. But still many people would take this deal, which fits just nicely into the theme of Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T10:56:39-08:00","id":1061289,"title":"","content":"Just another reason why Infernalists are better off than Thralls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T15:26:45-08:00","id":1061359,"title":"","content":"Well you could always go to the midnight circus from what i understand if you get a job there you can live for ever!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T05:54:40-07:00","id":1061796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1060868-means-of-extending-mortal-life?p=1061289#post1061289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just another reason why Infernalists are better off than Thralls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mainly depends on your infernal master. Ahrimal ain't no Belial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}